WEBVTT

observation-01
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:07.200
Start with hand hygiene.

observation-02
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:14.000
Observe the periorbital area, eyelids and eyes, noting any abnormalities.

observation-03
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:24.400
Prepare the Arclight by selecting the brightest light setting and pushing both lens racks fully up. Use a quiet, dim room.

observation-04a
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Position the sight hole close to your eye.

observation-04b
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.000
Do not shine the light into your own eye.

observation-04c
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.500
Do not hold the Arclight sideways.

observation-05
00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:49.100
At arm's length, ask the patient to look at the light and observe both eyes together.

observation-06
00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:55.200
The reflexes should be equally bright and similar in colour; asymmetry is abnormal.

positioning-01
00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:08.300
Ask the patient to fix on a distant target. Make sure they are not looking at you or at the light itself.

positioning-02
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:21.200
Use your right hand and right eye for the patient's right eye and your left hand and left eye for the left eye.

positioning-03
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:34.400
Start with your feet close to the patient and lean back. Identify the fundal reflex, then follow it in along a horizontal path 10 to 15 degrees temporal to the pupil.

positioning-04
00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:43.400
As you get close, the optic disc should come into view. Move closer for a wider, steadier view.

positioning-05
00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:53.200
Keep the Arclight aligned with the patient's eye and do not move it up or down. If you lose the disc, follow a major branch back to it.

features-01
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:05.000
At the optic disc, comment on how distinct its margin is.

features-02
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:13.500
Comment on the colour of the neuroretinal rim and the cup-to-disc ratio.

features-03
00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:24.620
A healthy disc has clear margins and a rim. Patients with any swelling, pale colour or increased cupping should be referred.

examine-01
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:33.700
Before examining the fovea, dilate the pupil. Otherwise, fixation on the light constricts it and obscures the view.

examine-02
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:38.000
Start at the optic disc.

examine-03
00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:56.400
Follow each of the four main retinal vessel branches. Start at the optic disc, follow one branch, return to the optic disc and then follow the next branch. Repeat this for all four branches.

examine-04
00:02:56.600 --> 00:03:03.050
Finish at the macula and fovea, then repeat the examination in the other eye.
